cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AgentEsc: A Taxonomy of Privilege-Escalation Threats in
  Tool-Calling and MCP-Based Agent Systems
message: >-
  If you use this taxonomy or benchmark, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aditya
    family-names: Mehra
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8307-9398'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/AddyM/agentesc'
url: 'https://github.com/AddyM/agentesc'
abstract: >-
  AgentEsc is an open taxonomy and benchmark for privilege-escalation
  threats in agentic AI systems that use tool-calling, the Model
  Context Protocol (MCP), or multi-agent orchestration. It provides a
  five-class taxonomy with fifteen testable sub-techniques, a
  declarative scenario schema, and metrics (Escalation Success Rate,
  Detection Rate, Containment Rate) evaluated across a defense ladder,
  enabling reproducible measurement of authorization-boundary
  vulnerabilities in agent frameworks.
keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - AI security
  - privilege escalation
  - tool-calling
  - Model Context Protocol
  - multi-agent systems
  - trustworthy machine learning
  - LLM security
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-07-12'
